166
00:20:53.212 --> 00:20:55.123
<v c-3po>Actually, there's not much to tell.</v>

167
00:20:55.214 --> 00:20:58.877
<v c-3po>I'm not much more than an interpreter and not very good at telling stories.</v>

168
00:20:58.967 --> 00:21:02.050
<v c-3po>Well, not at making them interesting, anyway.</v>

169
00:21:02.137 --> 00:21:04.048
<v luke>Well, my little friend,</v>

170
00:21:04.139 --> 00:21:06.221
<v luke>you got something jammed in here real good.</v>

171
00:21:06.308 --> 00:21:07.798
<v luke>Were you on a starcruiser or...</v>

172
00:21:08.644 --> 00:21:11.727
<v leia>Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi. You're my only hope.</v>

173
00:21:11.814 --> 00:21:13.475
<v luke>What's this?</v>

174
00:21:13.565 --> 00:21:16.682
<v c-3po>"What is what"? He asked you a question. What is that?</v>

175
00:21:16.777 --> 00:21:20.736
<v leia>Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi. You're my only hope.</v>

176
00:21:24.117 --> 00:21:28.076
<v leia>Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi. You're my only hope.</v>

177
00:21:30.582 --> 00:21:32.743
<v c-3po>Oh. He says it's nothing, sir, merely a malfunction.</v>

178
00:21:32.835 --> 00:21:34.700
<v c-3po>Old data. Pay it no mind.</v>

179
00:21:34.795 --> 00:21:37.161
<v luke>Who is she? She's beautiful.</v>

180
00:21:37.256 --> 00:21:40.669
<v c-3po>I'm afraid I'm not quite sure, sir.</v>

181
00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:42.966
<v c-3po>I think she was a passenger on our last voyage.</v>

182
00:21:43.053 --> 00:21:45.044
<v c-3po>A person of some importance, I believe.</v>

183
00:21:45.138 --> 00:21:47.504
<v c-3po>Our captain was...</v>
<v luke>Is there any more to this recording?</v>

184
00:21:49.685 --> 00:21:52.848
<v c-3po>Behave yourself, r2. You're going to get us into trouble.</v>

185
00:21:52.938 --> 00:21:55.680
<v c-3po>It's all right. You can trust him. He's our new master.</v>

186
00:21:55.774 --> 00:21:57.435
You're my only hope.

187
00:21:58.819 --> 00:22:01.856
<v c-3po>He says he's the property of Obi-Wan Kenobi,</v>

188
00:22:01.947 --> 00:22:03.483
<v c-3po>a resident of these parts,</v>

189
00:22:03.574 --> 00:22:05.280
<v c-3po>and it's a private message for him.</v>

190
00:22:05.367 --> 00:22:07.699
<v c-3po>Quite frankly, sir, I don't know what he's talking about.</v>

191
00:22:07.786 --> 00:22:09.526
<v c-3po>Our last master was captain antilles.</v>

192
00:22:09.621 --> 00:22:11.282
<v c-3po>But with all we've been through,</v>

193
00:22:11.373 --> 00:22:14.206
<v c-3po>this little r2 unit has become a bit eccentric.</v>

194
00:22:14.751 --> 00:22:17.663
<v luke>Obi-Wan Kenobi. I wonder if he means old Ben Kenobi.</v>

195
00:22:17.754 --> 00:22:20.461
<v c-3po>I beg your pardon, sir, but do you know what he's talking about?</v>

196
00:22:20.549 --> 00:22:23.006
<v luke>I don't know anyone named Obi-Wan,</v>

197
00:22:23.635 --> 00:22:25.751
<v luke>but old Ben lives out beyond the dune sea.</v>

198
00:22:25.846 --> 00:22:27.677
<v luke>He's kind of a strange old hermit.</v>

199
00:22:28.849 --> 00:22:30.840
<v luke>I wonder who she is.</v>

200
00:22:30.934 --> 00:22:33.971
<v luke>Sounds like she's in trouble. I better play back the whole thing.</v>

201
00:22:37.482 --> 00:22:40.895
<v c-3po>He says the restraining bolt has short-circuited his recording system.</v>

202
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.356
<v c-3po>He suggests that if you remove the bolt,</v>

203
00:22:43.447 --> 00:22:46.359
<v c-3po>he might be able to play back the entire recording.</v>

204
00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:48.782
<v luke>Oh, yeah. Well...</v>

205
00:22:48.869 --> 00:22:52.407
<v luke>I guess you're too small to run away on me if I take this off.</v>

206
00:22:52.497 --> 00:22:53.657
<v luke>Okay.</v>

207
00:22:56.418 --> 00:22:58.033
<v luke>There you go.</v>

208
00:22:59.713 --> 00:23:03.251
<v luke>Wait a minute. Where'd she go? Bring her back. Play back the entire message.</v>

209
00:23:03.342 --> 00:23:04.342
<v c-3po>"What message"?</v>

210
00:23:05.135 --> 00:23:06.591
The one you've just been playing.

211
00:23:06.678 --> 00:23:08.794
<v c-3po>The one you're carrying inside your rusty innards.</v>

212
00:23:08.889 --> 00:23:11.255
<v beru>Luke! Luke!</v>

213
00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:13.557
<v luke>I'll be right there, aunt beru.</v>

214
00:23:13.685 --> 00:23:16.802
<v c-3po>I'm sorry, sir, but he appears to have picked up a slight flutter.</v>

215
00:23:16.897 --> 00:23:20.355
<v luke>Here. See what you can do with him. I'll be right back.</v>

216
00:23:23.028 --> 00:23:25.519
<v c-3po>Just you reconsider playing that message for him.</v>

217
00:23:27.032 --> 00:23:29.364
<v c-3po>No, I don't think he likes you at all.</v>

218
00:23:29.451 --> 00:23:31.692
<v c-3po>No, I don't like you either.</v>

219
00:23:40.545 --> 00:23:43.287
<v luke>You know, I think that r2 unit we bought might have been stolen.</v>

220
00:23:43.382 --> 00:23:44.462
<v owen>What makes you think that?</v>

221
00:23:44.549 --> 00:23:47.165
<v luke>I stumbled across a recording while I was cleaning him.</v>

222
00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:50.002
<v luke>He says he belongs to someone called Obi-Wan Kenobi.</v>

223
00:23:52.599 --> 00:23:55.932
<v luke>I thought he might have meant old Ben. Do you know what he's talking about?</v>

224
00:23:58.689 --> 00:24:00.225
<v luke>I wonder if he's related to Ben.</v>

225
00:24:00.315 --> 00:24:02.101
<v owen>That wizard's just a crazy old man.</v>

226
00:24:03.276 --> 00:24:05.562
<v owen>Tomorrow, I want you to take that r2 unit to anchorhead</v>

227
00:24:05.654 --> 00:24:07.064
<v owen>and have its memory erased.</v>

228
00:24:07.155 --> 00:24:09.316
<v owen>That'll be the end of it. It belongs to us now.</v>

229
00:24:11.076 --> 00:24:14.113
<v luke>But what if this Obi-Wan comes looking for him?</v>

230
00:24:14.204 --> 00:24:15.944
<v owen>He won't.</v>

231
00:24:16.039 --> 00:24:17.995
<v owen>I don't think he exists anymore.</v>

232
00:24:18.083 --> 00:24:19.914
<v owen>He died about the same time as your father.</v>

233
00:24:20.293 --> 00:24:23.000
<v luke>He knew my father?</v>
<v owen>I told you to forget it.</v>

234
00:24:24.131 --> 00:24:27.715
<v owen>Your only concern is to prepare those new droids for tomorrow.</v>

235
00:24:27.801 --> 00:24:30.133
<v owen>In the morning, I want them up there on the south Ridge,</v>

236
00:24:30.220 --> 00:24:31.505
<v owen>working on those condensers.</v>

237
00:24:31.596 --> 00:24:33.086
<v luke>Yes, sir.</v>

238
00:24:34.474 --> 00:24:37.011
<v luke>I think those new droids are gonna work out fine.</v>

239
00:24:37.102 --> 00:24:40.686
<v luke>In fact, I was also thinking about our agreement,</v>

240
00:24:40.772 --> 00:24:42.512
<v luke>about me staying on another season.</v>

241
00:24:44.526 --> 00:24:46.062
<v luke>And if these new droids do work out,</v>

242
00:24:46.153 --> 00:24:48.644
<v luke>I want to transmit my application to the academy this year.</v>

243
00:24:49.156 --> 00:24:51.112
<v owen>You mean the next semester before the harvest?</v>

244
00:24:51.199 --> 00:24:53.110
<v luke>Sure. There's more than enough droids.</v>

245
00:24:53.201 --> 00:24:55.192
<v owen>Harvest is when I need you the most.</v>

246
00:24:55.287 --> 00:24:57.278
<v owen>It's only one season more.</v>

247
00:24:57.372 --> 00:24:59.078
<v owen>This year we'll make enough on the harvest</v>

248
00:24:59.166 --> 00:25:00.906
<v owen>that I'll be able to hire some more hands</v>

249
00:25:01.001 --> 00:25:02.957
<v owen>and then you can go to the academy next year.</v>

250
00:25:03.879 --> 00:25:05.870
<v owen>You must understand I need you here, Luke.</v>

251
00:25:05.964 --> 00:25:08.876
<v luke>But it's a whole 'nother year.</v>
<v owen>It's only one more season.</v>

252
00:25:08.967 --> 00:25:11.049
<v luke>That's what you said when Biggs and tank left.</v>

253
00:25:11.136 --> 00:25:13.593
<v beru>Where are you going?</v>
<v luke>Looks like I'm going nowhere.</v>

254
00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:15.545
<v luke>I have to go finish cleaning those droids.</v>

255
00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:19.053
<v beru>Owen, he can't stay here forever. Most of his friends have gone.</v>

256
00:25:19.352 --> 00:25:21.559
<v beru>It means so much to him.</v>

257
00:25:21.646 --> 00:25:24.183
<v owen>I'l make it up to him next year. I promise.</v>

258
00:25:25.859 --> 00:25:29.852
<v beru>Luke's just not a farmer, Owen. He has too much of his father in him.</v>

259
00:25:30.322 --> 00:25:32.108
<v owen>That's what I'm afraid of.</v>

260
00:26:21.331 --> 00:26:24.448
<v luke>What are you doing hiding back there?</v>
<v c-3po>It wasn't my fault, sir.</v>

261
00:26:24.543 --> 00:26:26.283
<v c-3po>Please don't deactivate me.</v>

262
00:26:26.378 --> 00:26:29.120
<v c-3po>I told him not to go, but he's faulty, malfunctioning.</v>

263
00:26:29.214 --> 00:26:32.456
<v c-3po>Kept babbling on about his mission.</v>
<v luke>Oh, no.</v>

264
00:26:40.892 --> 00:26:43.304
<v c-3po>That r2 unit has always been a problem.</v>

265
00:26:43.728 --> 00:26:45.969
<v c-3po>These astro droids are getting quite out of hand.</v>

266
00:26:46.064 --> 00:26:48.271
<v c-3po>Even I can't understand their logic at times.</v>

267
00:26:48.358 --> 00:26:51.065
<v luke>How could I be so stupid? He's nowhere in sight.</v>

268
00:26:51.528 --> 00:26:52.528
<v luke>Blast it!</v>

269
00:26:52.612 --> 00:26:54.853
<v c-3po>Pardon me, sir, but couldn't we go after him?</v>

270
00:26:54.948 --> 00:26:56.813
<v luke>It's too dangerous with the sandpeople around.</v>

271
00:26:56.908 --> 00:26:58.188
<v luke>We'll have to wait till morning.</v>

272
00:26:58.243 --> 00:27:00.199
<v owen>Luke, I'm shutting the power down.</v>

273
00:27:00.287 --> 00:27:02.824
<v luke>All right. I'll be there in a few minutes.</v>

274
00:27:02.914 --> 00:27:05.326
<v luke>Boy, am I gonna get it.</v>

275
00:27:05.417 --> 00:27:07.270
<v luke>You know, that little droid's gonna cause me a lot of trouble.</v>

276
00:27:07.294 --> 00:27:09.125
<v c-3po>Oh, he excels at that, sir.</v>

277
00:27:09.212 --> 00:27:11.703
(Sighs) Come on.

278
00:27:20.265 --> 00:27:21.596
I uke?

279
00:27:22.726 --> 00:27:23.841
I uke?

280
00:27:24.936 --> 00:27:26.096
<v owen>Luke!</v>

281
00:27:32.277 --> 00:27:34.188
<v owen>Have you seen Luke this morning?</v>

282
00:27:34.279 --> 00:27:37.692
<v beru>He said he had some things to do before he started today, so he left early.</v>

283
00:27:37.782 --> 00:27:41.400
<v beru>[Did he take those new droids with him? =] Think so.</v>

284
00:27:41.494 --> 00:27:44.361
<v owen>He better have those units in the south range repaired by midday</v>

285
00:27:44.456 --> 00:27:45.992
<v owen>or there'll be hell to pay.</v>

286
00:27:47.125 --> 00:27:49.707
<v luke>There's a droid on the scanner. Dead ahead.</v>

287
00:27:49.794 --> 00:27:52.786
<v luke>It might be our little r2 unit. Hit the accelerator.</v>

288
00:28:14.945 --> 00:28:17.027
<v luke>Hey, whoa just where do you think you're going?</v>

289
00:28:17.113 --> 00:28:20.071
<v c-3po>Master Luke is your rightful owner now.</v>

290
00:28:20.158 --> 00:28:23.150
<v c-3po>We'll have no more of this Obi-Wan Kenobi gibberish.</v>

291
00:28:24.412 --> 00:28:26.073
<v c-3po>Don't talk to me of your mission either.</v>

292
00:28:26.164 --> 00:28:29.247
<v c-3po>You're fortunate he doesn't blast you into a million pieces right here.</v>

293
00:28:29.334 --> 00:28:32.201
No. It's all right, but I think we'd better go.

294
00:28:32.295 --> 00:28:34.581
<v luke>(Whistle whistle) What's wrong with him now?</v>

295
00:28:34.881 --> 00:28:37.748
<v c-3po>There are several creatures approaching from the southeast.</v>

296
00:28:37.842 --> 00:28:40.299
<v luke>Sandpeople. Or worse.</v>

297
00:28:41.680 --> 00:28:43.261
<v luke>Come on. Let's go have a look.</v>

298
00:28:43.348 --> 00:28:44.463
<v luke>Come on.</v>

299
00:28:47.185 --> 00:28:50.928
<v luke>Well, there are two banthas down there, but I don't see any...</v>

300
00:28:51.022 --> 00:28:52.808
<v luke>Wait a second.</v>

301
00:28:52.899 --> 00:28:55.356
<v luke>They're sandpeople, all right. I can see one of them now.</v>

302
00:30:10.435 --> 00:30:11.595
<v obi-wan>Hello there.</v>

303
00:30:14.272 --> 00:30:17.935
<v obi-wan>Come here, my little friend. Don't be afraid.</v>

304
00:30:20.153 --> 00:30:21.768
<v obi-wan>Don't worry. He'll be all right.</v>

305
00:30:27.952 --> 00:30:30.443
<v obi-wan>Rest easy, son. You've had a busy day.</v>

306
00:30:31.289 --> 00:30:34.201
<v obi-wan>You're fortunate to be all in one piece.</v>

307
00:30:37.504 --> 00:30:39.745
<v luke>Ben? Ben Kenobi?</v>

308
00:30:39.839 --> 00:30:41.875
<v luke>Boy, am I glad to see you.</v>

309
00:30:41.966 --> 00:30:45.003
<v obi-wan>The jundland wastes are not to be traveled lightly.</v>

310
00:30:48.139 --> 00:30:52.303
<v obi-wan>Tell me, young Luke, what brings you out this far?</v>

311
00:30:52.394 --> 00:30:53.930
<v luke>This little droid.</v>

312
00:30:55.647 --> 00:30:57.638
<v luke>I think he's searching for his former master,</v>

313
00:30:57.732 --> 00:30:59.939
<v luke>but I've never seen such devotion in a droid before.</v>

314
00:31:01.903 --> 00:31:04.986
<v luke>He claims to be the property of an Obi-Wan Kenobi.</v>

315
00:31:05.073 --> 00:31:07.689
<v luke>Is he a relative of yours? Do you know who he's talking about?</v>

316
00:31:09.244 --> 00:31:10.825
<v obi-wan>Obi-Wan Kenobi?</v>

317
00:31:13.331 --> 00:31:15.242
<v obi-wan>Obi-Wan.</v>

318
00:31:15.708 --> 00:31:19.917
<v obi-wan>Now, that's a name I've not heard in a long time.</v>

319
00:31:20.505 --> 00:31:22.336
<v obi-wan>A long time.</v>

320
00:31:23.508 --> 00:31:26.420
<v luke>I think my uncle knows him. He said he was dead.</v>

321
00:31:26.511 --> 00:31:28.342
<v obi-wan>Oh, he's not dead.</v>

322
00:31:28.430 --> 00:31:29.545
<v obi-wan>Not yet.</v>

323
00:31:29.973 --> 00:31:33.136
<v luke>You know him?</v>
<v obi-wan>Well, of course I know him.</v>

324
00:31:33.226 --> 00:31:34.591
<v obi-wan>He's me.</v>

325
00:31:36.729 --> 00:31:40.062
<v obi-wan>I haven't gone by the name of Obi-Wan</v>

326
00:31:40.150 --> 00:31:42.766
<v obi-wan>since, oh, before you were born.</v>

327
00:31:42.861 --> 00:31:44.522
<v luke>Well, then the droid does belong to you.</v>

328
00:31:44.904 --> 00:31:47.236
<v obi-wan>I don't seem to remember ever owning a droid.</v>

329
00:31:49.492 --> 00:31:51.232
<v obi-wan>Very interesting.</v>

330
00:31:52.579 --> 00:31:55.116
<v obi-wan>I think we better get indoors.</v>

331
00:31:55.206 --> 00:31:57.868
<v obi-wan>The sandpeople are easily startled,</v>

332
00:31:57.959 --> 00:32:00.792
<v obi-wan>but they'll soon be back, and in greater numbers.</v>

333
00:32:03.756 --> 00:32:05.041
Ipo.

334
00:32:14.392 --> 00:32:17.054
<v c-3po>Where am 1? I must have taken a bad step.</v>

335
00:32:18.605 --> 00:32:21.813
<v luke>Can you stand? We've gotta get out of here before the sandpeople return.</v>

336
00:32:21.900 --> 00:32:24.607
<v c-3po>I don't think I can make it. You go on, master Luke.</v>

337
00:32:24.736 --> 00:32:28.820
<v c-3po>There's no sense in you risking yourself on my account. I'm done for.</v>

338
00:32:29.782 --> 00:32:31.693
<v luke>No, you're not. What kind of talk is that?</v>

339
00:32:31.784 --> 00:32:33.740
<v obi-wan>Quickly. They're on the move.</v>

340
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:42.367
<v luke>My father didn't fight in the wars. He was a navigator on a spice freighter.</v>

341
00:32:42.462 --> 00:32:44.293
<v obi-wan>That's what your uncle told you.</v>

342
00:32:44.380 --> 00:32:46.211
<v obi-wan>He didn't hold with your father's ideals.</v>

343
00:32:46.299 --> 00:32:49.416
<v obi-wan>Thought he should have stayed here and not gotten involved.</v>

344
00:32:50.136 --> 00:32:52.502
<v luke>You fought in the clone wars? Yes.</v>

345
00:32:52.972 --> 00:32:56.635
<v obi-wan>I was once a jedi knight, the same as your father.</v>

346
00:32:59.020 --> 00:33:00.351
<v luke>I wish I'd known him.</v>

347
00:33:00.438 --> 00:33:03.180
<v obi-wan>He was the best starpilot in the galaxy</v>

348
00:33:04.275 --> 00:33:06.106
<v obi-wan>and a cunning warrior.</v>

349
00:33:06.194 --> 00:33:09.106
<v obi-wan>I understand you've become quite a good pilot yourself.</v>

350
00:33:10.990 --> 00:33:13.276
<v obi-wan>And he was a good friend.</v>

351
00:33:13.952 --> 00:33:15.067
<v obi-wan>Which reminds me...</v>

352
00:33:16.162 --> 00:33:18.153
<v obi-wan>I have something here for you.</v>

353
00:33:23.378 --> 00:33:25.494
<v obi-wan>but your uncle wouldn't allow it.</v>

354
00:33:26.464 --> 00:33:28.580
<v obi-wan>He feared you might follow old Obi-Wan</v>

355
00:33:28.675 --> 00:33:32.167
<v obi-wan>on some damn-fool idealistic crusade, like your father did.</v>

356
00:33:32.262 --> 00:33:35.129
<v c-3po>Sir, if you'll not be needing me, I'll close down for a while.</v>

357
00:33:35.223 --> 00:33:36.804
<v luke>Sure. Go ahead.</v>

358
00:33:39.477 --> 00:33:42.890
<v luke>What is it?</v>
<v obi-wan>Your father's lightsaber.</v>

359
00:33:43.648 --> 00:33:45.309
<v obi-wan>This is the weapon of a jedi knight.</v>

360
00:33:46.359 --> 00:33:49.522
<v obi-wan>Not as clumsy or random as a blaster.</v>

361
00:33:50.196 --> 00:33:52.437
<v obi-wan>An elegant weapon</v>

362
00:33:52.532 --> 00:33:55.524
<v obi-wan>for a more civilized age.</v>

363
00:33:57.412 --> 00:33:59.778
<v obi-wan>For over a thousand generations, the jedi knights</v>

364
00:33:59.872 --> 00:34:03.956
<v obi-wan>were the guardians of peace and justice in the old Republic</v>

365
00:34:04.460 --> 00:34:06.872
<v obi-wan>before the dark times,</v>

366
00:34:06.963 --> 00:34:08.499
<v obi-wan>before the empire.</v>

367
00:34:11.718 --> 00:34:13.424
<v luke>How did my father die?</v>

368
00:34:15.888 --> 00:34:18.425
<v obi-wan>A young jedi named Darth Vader,</v>

369
00:34:18.516 --> 00:34:21.007
<v obi-wan>who was a pupil of mine until he turned to evil,</v>

370
00:34:21.853 --> 00:34:25.186
<v obi-wan>helped the empire hunt down and destroy the jedi knights.</v>

371
00:34:27.025 --> 00:34:29.437
<v obi-wan>He betrayed and murdered your father.</v>

372
00:34:31.195 --> 00:34:33.527
<v obi-wan>Now the jedi are all but extinct.</v>

373
00:34:34.699 --> 00:34:38.487
<v obi-wan>Vader was seduced by the dark side of the force.</v>

374
00:34:39.287 --> 00:34:41.323
<v luke>The force?</v>

375
00:34:41.414 --> 00:34:44.451
<v obi-wan>The force is what gives a jedi his power.</v>

376
00:34:44.542 --> 00:34:47.124
<v obi-wan>It's an energy field created by all living things.</v>

377
00:34:47.211 --> 00:34:49.748
<v obi-wan>It surrounds us and penetrates us.</v>

378
00:34:49.881 --> 00:34:51.963
<v obi-wan>It binds the galaxy together.</v>

379
00:34:58.931 --> 00:35:02.014
<v obi-wan>Now, let's see if we can't figure out what you are, my little friend,</v>

380
00:35:02.769 --> 00:35:04.851
<v obi-wan>and where you come from.</v>

381
00:35:04.937 --> 00:35:08.145
I saw part of a message... =l seem to have found it.

382
00:35:08.232 --> 00:35:12.566
<v leia>General Kenobi, years ago you served my father in the clone wars.</v>

383
00:35:12.945 --> 00:35:16.062
<v leia>Now he begs you to help him in his struggle against the empire.</v>

384
00:35:16.157 --> 00:35:19.490
<v leia>I regret that I am unable to present my father's request in person.</v>

385
00:35:19.577 --> 00:35:21.238
<v leia>But my ship has fallen under attack</v>

386
00:35:21.329 --> 00:35:23.991
<v leia>and I'm afraid my mission to bring you to alderaan has failed.</v>

387
00:35:24.082 --> 00:35:27.165
<v leia>I have placed information vital to the survival of the rebellion</v>

388
00:35:27.251 --> 00:35:29.458
<v leia>into the memory systems of this r2 unit</v>

389
00:35:29.545 --> 00:35:31.456
<v leia>my father will know how to retrieve it.</v>

390
00:35:31.923 --> 00:35:35.666
<v leia>You must see this droid safely delivered to him on alderaan.</v>

391
00:35:35.760 --> 00:35:37.421
<v leia>This is our most desperate hour.</v>

392
00:35:38.179 --> 00:35:41.467
<v leia>Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi. You're my only hope.</v>

393
00:35:56.447 --> 00:36:00.611
<v obi-wan>You must learn the ways of the force if you're to come with me to alderaan.</v>

394
00:36:01.327 --> 00:36:02.692
<v luke>Alderaan?</v>

395
00:36:02.787 --> 00:36:04.027
<v luke>I'm not going to alderaan.</v>

396
00:36:04.122 --> 00:36:06.534
<v luke>I've gotta get home. It's late. I'm in for it as it is.</v>

397
00:36:06.624 --> 00:36:09.081
<v obi-wan>I need your help, Luke. She needs your help.</v>

398
00:36:09.585 --> 00:36:12.247
<v obi-wan>I'm getting too old for this sort of thing.</v>

399
00:36:16.843 --> 00:36:20.210
<v luke>I can't get involved. I've got work to do.</v>

400
00:36:21.013 --> 00:36:22.878
<v luke>It's not that I like the empire. I hate it.</v>

401
00:36:22.974 --> 00:36:25.556
<v luke>But there's nothing I can do about it right now.</v>

402
00:36:27.019 --> 00:36:30.637
<v luke>It's all such a long way from here.</v>
<v obi-wan>That's your uncle talking.</v>

403
00:36:30.857 --> 00:36:34.566
<v luke>Oh, boy. My uncle. How am I ever gonna explain this?</v>

404
00:36:34.652 --> 00:36:36.358
<v obi-wan>Learn about the force, Luke.</v>

405
00:36:43.494 --> 00:36:46.236
<v luke>Look, I can take you as far as anchorhead.</v>

406
00:36:46.330 --> 00:36:49.663
<v luke>You can get a transport there to mos eisley or wherever you're going.</v>

407
00:36:51.002 --> 00:36:53.994
<v obi-wan>You must do what you feel is right, of course.</v>

408
00:37:01.554 --> 00:37:05.172
<v tagge>Until this battle station is fully operational, we are vulnerable.</v>

409
00:37:05.266 --> 00:37:07.723
<v tagge>The rebel alliance is too well equipped.</v>

410
00:37:07.810 --> 00:37:09.471
<v tagge>They're more dangerous than you realize.</v>

411
00:37:09.562 --> 00:37:12.429
<v motti>Dangerous to your starfleet, commander,</v>

412
00:37:12.523 --> 00:37:14.263
<v motti>not to this battle station.</v>

413
00:37:14.358 --> 00:37:17.942
<v tagge>The rebellion will continue to gain support in the imperial senate...</v>

414
00:37:18.029 --> 00:37:22.363
<v tarkin>The imperial senate will no longer be of any concern to us.</v>

415
00:37:22.450 --> 00:37:26.614
<v tarkin>I've just received word that the emperor has dissolved the council permanently.</v>

416
00:37:26.704 --> 00:37:30.697
<v tarkin>The last remnants of the old Republic have been swept away.</v>

417
00:37:30.792 --> 00:37:32.453
<v tagge>That's impossible.</v>

418
00:37:32.543 --> 00:37:35.159
<v tagge>How will the emperor maintain control without the bureaucracy?</v>

419
00:37:35.254 --> 00:37:40.044
<v tarkin>The regional governors now have direct control over their territories.</v>

420
00:37:40.134 --> 00:37:43.877
<v tarkin>Fear will keep the local systems in line.</v>

421
00:37:44.013 --> 00:37:46.095
<v tarkin>Fear of this battle station.</v>

422
00:37:46.182 --> 00:37:47.367
<v tagge>And what of the rebellion?</v>

423
00:37:47.391 --> 00:37:50.633
<v tagge>If the rebels have obtained a complete technical readout of this station,</v>

424
00:37:50.728 --> 00:37:52.639
<v tagge>it is possible, however unlikely,</v>

425
00:37:52.730 --> 00:37:54.891
<v tagge>that they might find a weakness and exploit it.</v>

426
00:37:55.483 --> 00:37:59.226
<v vader>The plans you refer to will soon be back in our hands.</v>

427
00:37:59.320 --> 00:38:03.563
<v motti>Any attack made by the rebels against this station would be a useless gesture,</v>

428
00:38:03.658 --> 00:38:05.740
<v motti>no matter what technical data they've obtained.</v>

429
00:38:05.827 --> 00:38:09.445
<v motti>This station is now the ultimate power in the universe.</v>

430
00:38:10.122 --> 00:38:11.828
<v motti>I suggest we use it.</v>

431
00:38:11.916 --> 00:38:16.159
<v vader>Don't be too proud of this technological terror you've constructed.</v>

432
00:38:16.254 --> 00:38:19.667
<v vader>The ability to destroy a planet is insignificant</v>

433
00:38:19.757 --> 00:38:21.588
<v vader>next to the power of the force.</v>

434
00:38:21.676 --> 00:38:25.168
<v motti>Don't try to frighten us with your sorcerer's ways, lord vader.</v>

435
00:38:25.263 --> 00:38:28.096
<v motti>Your sad devotion to that ancient religion</v>

436
00:38:28.182 --> 00:38:30.764
<v motti>has not helped you conjure up the stolen data tapes</v>

437
00:38:31.269 --> 00:38:34.261
<v motti>or given you clairvoyance enough to find the rebels' hidden fortress...</v>

438
00:38:41.904 --> 00:38:44.520
<v vader>I find your lack of faith disturbing.</v>

439
00:38:45.950 --> 00:38:48.566
<v tarkin>Enough of this. Vader, release him.</v>

440
00:38:48.661 --> 00:38:50.117
<v vader>As you wish.</v>

441
00:38:52.498 --> 00:38:54.454
<v tarkin>This bickering is pointless.</v>

442
00:38:55.626 --> 00:38:59.369
<v tarkin>Lord vader will provide us with the location of the rebel fortress</v>

443
00:38:59.463 --> 00:39:02.045
<v tarkin>by the time this station is operational.</v>

444
00:39:02.133 --> 00:39:06.126
<v tarkin>We will then crush the rebellion with one swift stroke.</v>

445
00:39:13.144 --> 00:39:15.100
<v luke>It looks like the sandpeople did this, all right.</v>

446
00:39:15.187 --> 00:39:16.802
<v luke>There's gaffi sticks, bantha tracks.</v>

447
00:39:16.898 --> 00:39:19.731
<v luke>I've just never heard of them hitting anything this big before.</v>

448
00:39:19.817 --> 00:39:22.729
<v obi-wan>They didn't, but we are meant to think they did.</v>

449
00:39:22.820 --> 00:39:24.731
<v obi-wan>These tracks are side-by-side.</v>

450
00:39:24.822 --> 00:39:28.940
<v obi-wan>Sandpeople always ride single file to hide their numbers.</v>

451
00:39:29.035 --> 00:39:31.902
<v luke>These are the same jawas that sold us r2 and 3po.</v>

452
00:39:31.996 --> 00:39:36.786
<v obi-wan>And these blast points, too accurate for sandpeople.</v>

453
00:39:36.876 --> 00:39:40.789
<v obi-wan>Only imperial stormtroopers are so precise.</v>

454
00:39:40.880 --> 00:39:43.496
<v luke>But why would imperial troops want to slaughter jawas?</v>

455
00:39:48.846 --> 00:39:50.256
<v luke>If they traced the robots here,</v>

456
00:39:50.348 --> 00:39:52.134
<v luke>they may have learned who they sold them to</v>

457
00:39:52.224 --> 00:39:54.089
<v luke>and that would lead them back home.</v>

458
00:39:54.185 --> 00:39:55.220
<v obi-wan>Wait, Luke.</v>

459
00:39:55.478 --> 00:39:57.469
<v obi-wan>It's too dangerous.</v>

460
00:40:21.504 --> 00:40:23.369
<v luke>Uncle Owen.</v>

461
00:40:23.464 --> 00:40:25.295
<v luke>Aunt beru.</v>

462
00:40:25.424 --> 00:40:26.789
<v luke>Uncle Owen.</v>

463
00:41:17.018 --> 00:41:22.604
<v vader>Now, your highness, we will discuss the location of your hidden rebel base.</v>

464
00:42:05.649 --> 00:42:07.935
<v obi-wan>There's nothing you could have done, had you been there.</v>

465
00:42:08.819 --> 00:42:10.730
<v obi-wan>You'd have been killed too,</v>

466
00:42:10.821 --> 00:42:13.608
<v obi-wan>and the droids would now be in the hands of the empire.</v>

467
00:42:15.326 --> 00:42:17.942
<v luke>I want to come with you to alderaan.</v>

468
00:42:18.037 --> 00:42:20.073
<v luke>There's nothing for me here now.</v>

469
00:42:20.164 --> 00:42:23.156
<v luke>I want to learn the ways of the force and become a jedi like my father.</v>

470
00:42:38.849 --> 00:42:41.261
<v obi-wan>Mos eisley spaceport.</v>

471
00:42:41.352 --> 00:42:46.938
<v obi-wan>You will never find a more wretched hive of scum and villainy.</v>

472
00:42:47.024 --> 00:42:48.514
<v obi-wan>We must be cautious.</v>

473
00:43:29.900 --> 00:43:31.811
<v role-stormtrooper>How long have you had these droids?</v>

474
00:43:31.902 --> 00:43:35.065
<v luke>About three or four seasons.</v>
<v obi-wan>They're up for sale if you want them.</v>

475
00:43:35.656 --> 00:43:37.066
<v role-stormtrooper>Let me see your identification.</v>

476
00:43:37.741 --> 00:43:40.483
<v obi-wan>You don't need to see his identification.</v>

477
00:43:40.786 --> 00:43:42.902
<v role-stormtrooper>We don't need to see his identification.</v>

478
00:43:42.997 --> 00:43:45.830
<v obi-wan>These aren't the droids you're looking for.</v>

479
00:43:45.916 --> 00:43:47.827
<v role-stormtrooper>These aren't the droids we're looking for.</v>

480
00:43:48.752 --> 00:43:51.084
<v obi-wan>He can go about his business.</v>

481
00:43:51.172 --> 00:43:54.414
<v role-stormtrooper>You can go about your business.</v>
<v obi-wan>Move along.</v>

482
00:43:54.758 --> 00:43:57.340
<v role-stormtrooper>Move along. Move along.</v>

483
00:44:13.444 --> 00:44:16.607
<v c-3po>I can't abide those jawas. Disgusting creatures.</v>

484
00:44:17.615 --> 00:44:19.480
<v luke>Go on, go on.</v>

485
00:44:20.784 --> 00:44:22.695
<v luke>I can't understand how we got by those troops.</v>

486
00:44:22.786 --> 00:44:24.117
<v luke>I thought we were dead.</v>

487
00:44:24.205 --> 00:44:28.574
<v obi-wan>The force can have a strong influence on the weak-minded.</v>

488
00:44:31.962 --> 00:44:33.148
<v luke>You really think we're gonna find</v>

489
00:44:33.172 --> 00:44:35.163
<v luke>a pilot here that'll take us to alderaan?</v>

490
00:44:35.257 --> 00:44:37.999
<v obi-wan>Most of the best freighter pilots are to be found here.</v>

491
00:44:38.093 --> 00:44:41.881
<v obi-wan>Only watch your step, this place can be a little rough.</v>

492
00:44:41.972 --> 00:44:43.678
<v luke>I'm ready for anything.</v>

493
00:44:47.478 --> 00:44:49.434
<v c-3po>Come along, r2.</v>

494
00:45:39.530 --> 00:45:43.068
<v role-bartender>Hey. We don't serve their kind here. What?</v>

495
00:45:43.158 --> 00:45:45.069
<v role-bartender>Your droids, they'll have to wait outside.</v>

496
00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:46.160
<v role-bartender>We don't want them here.</v>

497
00:45:46.245 --> 00:45:48.952
<v luke>Why don't you wait out by the speeder? We don't want any trouble.</v>

498
00:45:49.039 --> 00:45:50.700
<v c-3po>I heartily agree with you, sir.</v>

499
00:45:59.300 --> 00:46:01.791
Uh... I'll have one of those.

500
00:46:37.713 --> 00:46:40.580
<v role-man>He doesn't like you.</v>
<v luke>I'm sorry.</v>

501
00:46:41.759 --> 00:46:45.251
<v role-man>I don't like you either. You just watch yourself.</v>

502
00:46:45.429 --> 00:46:50.014
<v role-man>We're wanted men. I have the death sentence on 12 systems.</v>

503
00:46:50.100 --> 00:46:52.887
I'll be careful then. You'll be dead!

504
00:46:52.978 --> 00:46:54.934
<v obi-wan>This little one's not worth the effort.</v>

505
00:46:56.106 --> 00:46:57.562
<v obi-wan>Come, let me get you something.</v>

506
00:46:57.816 --> 00:46:58.851
Aah!

507
00:47:24.885 --> 00:47:26.625
I'm all right.

508
00:47:28.180 --> 00:47:32.765
<v obi-wan>Chewbacca here is first mate on a ship that might suit us.</v>

509
00:47:37.189 --> 00:47:39.225
<v c-3po>I don't like the look of this.</v>

510
00:47:54.039 --> 00:47:57.623
<v han>Han Solo. I'm captain of the millennium falcon.</v>

511
00:47:57.709 --> 00:48:00.951
<v han>Chewie here tells me you're looking for passage to the alderaan system.</v>

512
00:48:01.046 --> 00:48:03.412
<v obi-wan>Yes, indeed, if it's a fast ship.</v>

513
00:48:03.507 --> 00:48:07.796
<v han>Fast ship? You've never heard of the millennium falcon?</v>

514
00:48:07.886 --> 00:48:08.966
<v obi-wan>Should I have?</v>

515
00:48:09.054 --> 00:48:12.217
<v han>It's the ship that made the kessel run in less than 12 parsecs.</v>

516
00:48:14.268 --> 00:48:16.475
<v han>I've outrun imperial starships.</v>

517
00:48:16.562 --> 00:48:18.553
<v han>Not the local bulk cruisers, mind you.</v>

518
00:48:18.647 --> 00:48:20.808
<v han>I'm talking about the big corellian ships now.</v>

519
00:48:22.693 --> 00:48:25.605
<v han>She's fast enough for you, old man.</v>

520
00:48:25.696 --> 00:48:28.608
<v han>What's the cargo?</v>
<v obi-wan>Only passengers.</v>

521
00:48:28.699 --> 00:48:31.532
<v obi-wan>Myself, the boy, two droids...</v>

522
00:48:32.703 --> 00:48:34.614
<v obi-wan>And no questions asked.</v>

523
00:48:36.081 --> 00:48:37.787
<v han>What is it, some kind of local trouble?</v>

524
00:48:38.208 --> 00:48:43.043
<v obi-wan>Let's just say we'd like to avoid any imperial entanglements.</v>

525
00:48:44.423 --> 00:48:47.665
<v han>Well, that's the real trick, isn't it?</v>

526
00:48:47.759 --> 00:48:49.750
<v han>And it's gonna cost you something extra.</v>

527
00:48:51.054 --> 00:48:52.885
<v han>Ten thousand, all in advance.</v>

528
00:48:54.558 --> 00:48:55.889
<v luke>Ten thousand?</v>

529
00:48:57.186 --> 00:48:58.972
<v luke>We could almost buy our own ship for that.</v>

530
00:48:59.855 --> 00:49:02.062
<v han>But who's gonna fly it, kid? You?</v>

531
00:49:02.149 --> 00:49:04.231
<v luke>You bet I could. I'm not such a bad pilot, myself.</v>

532
00:49:04.318 --> 00:49:06.809
<v luke>We don't have to sit here and listen...</v>

533
00:49:07.404 --> 00:49:09.645
<v obi-wan>We can pay you 2,000 now,</v>

534
00:49:09.740 --> 00:49:13.073
<v obi-wan>plus 15 when we reach alderaan.</v>

535
00:49:13.994 --> 00:49:15.200
<v han>Seventeen?</v>

536
00:49:18.665 --> 00:49:20.997
<v han>Okay, you guys got yourselves a ship.</v>

537
00:49:21.084 --> 00:49:23.917
<v han>We'll leave as soon as you're ready. Docking bay 94.</v>

538
00:49:24.004 --> 00:49:25.540
<v obi-wan>Ninety-four.</v>

539
00:49:26.423 --> 00:49:30.507
<v han>Looks like somebody's beginning to take an interest in your handiwork.</v>

540
00:49:31.762 --> 00:49:33.593
<v role-stormtrooper>All right. We'll check it out.</v>

541
00:49:45.442 --> 00:49:49.026
<v han>Seventeen thousand. Those guys must really be desperate.</v>

542
00:49:49.112 --> 00:49:53.481
<v han>This could really save my neck. Get back to the ship, get it ready.</v>

543
00:49:53.575 --> 00:49:55.782
<v obi-wan>You'll have to sell your speeder.</v>
<v luke>That's okay.</v>

544
00:49:55.869 --> 00:49:58.485
<v luke>I'm never coming back to this planet again.</v>

545
00:50:01.124 --> 00:50:02.124
<v han>(In english) Yes, greedo.</v>

546
00:50:02.209 --> 00:50:04.416
<v han>As a matter of fact, I was just going to see your boss.</v>

547
00:50:04.503 --> 00:50:06.710
<v han>Tell jabba that I've got his money.</v>

548
00:50:19.977 --> 00:50:22.218
<v han>(In english) Yeah, but this time I've got the money.</v>

549
00:50:26.358 --> 00:50:29.225
<v han>(In english) I don't have it with me. Tell jabba...</v>

550
00:50:37.494 --> 00:50:38.972
<v han>(In english) Even I get boarded sometimes.</v>

551
00:50:38.996 --> 00:50:41.237
<v han>Do you think I had a choice?</v>

552
00:50:46.169 --> 00:50:47.579
<v han>(In english) Over my dead body.</v>

553
00:50:53.010 --> 00:50:54.341
<v han>(In english) I'll bet you have.</v>

554
00:51:08.358 --> 00:51:10.440
<v han>Sorry about the mess.</v>

555
00:51:19.620 --> 00:51:22.737
<v vader>Her resistance to the mind probe is considerable.</v>

556
00:51:22.831 --> 00:51:26.198
<v vader>It'll be some time before we can extract any information from her.</v>

557
00:51:26.293 --> 00:51:29.877
<v role-officer>The final checkout is completed. All systems are operational.</v>

558
00:51:29.963 --> 00:51:32.170
<v role-officer>What course shall we set?</v>

559
00:51:32.299 --> 00:51:36.042
<v tarkin>Perhaps she would respond to an alternative form of persuasion.</v>

560
00:51:36.136 --> 00:51:37.376
<v vader>What do you mean?</v>

561
00:51:37.471 --> 00:51:40.429
<v tarkin>I think it is time we demonstrated the full power of this station.</v>

562
00:51:40.515 --> 00:51:43.006
<v tarkin>Set your course for alderaan.</v>
<v role-stormtrooper>With pleasure.</v>

563
00:51:44.186 --> 00:51:46.222
<v c-3po>Lock the door, r2.</v>

564
00:51:48.315 --> 00:51:50.306
<v role-stormtrooper>All right. Check this side of the street.</v>

565
00:51:54.488 --> 00:51:57.150
<v role-stormtrooper>The door's locked. Move on to the next one.</v>

566
00:52:03.997 --> 00:52:06.955
<v c-3po>I would much rather have gone with master Luke than stay here with you.</v>

567
00:52:07.417 --> 00:52:11.001
<v c-3po>I don't know what this trouble is about, but I'm sure it must be your fault.</v>

568
00:52:11.088 --> 00:52:13.170
<v c-3po>You watch your language.</v>

569
00:52:15.676 --> 00:52:18.588
<v luke>All right. Give it to me. I'll take it.</v>

570
00:52:18.679 --> 00:52:22.263
<v luke>Look at this. Ever since the xp-38 came out, they just aren't in demand.</v>

571
00:52:22.349 --> 00:52:24.340
<v obi-wan>It'll be enough.</v>

572
00:52:47.082 --> 00:52:49.073
<v han>(In english) Right here, jabba.</v>

573
00:52:50.460 --> 00:52:51.870
<v han>I've been waitin' for you.</v>

574
00:52:55.799 --> 00:52:58.461
<v han>(In english) You didn't think I was gonna run, did you?</v>

575
00:53:08.812 --> 00:53:10.331
<v han>(In english) Jabba, next time you wanna talk to me,</v>

576
00:53:10.355 --> 00:53:11.515
<v han>come see me yourself.</v>

577
00:53:11.606 --> 00:53:13.096
<v han>Don't send one of these twerps.</v>

578
00:53:27.414 --> 00:53:30.827
<v han>(In english) Look, jabba, even I get boarded sometimes.</v>

579
00:53:31.668 --> 00:53:34.159
<v han>You think I had a choice?</v>

580
00:53:34.254 --> 00:53:36.165
<v han>But I got a nice, easy charter.</v>

581
00:53:36.256 --> 00:53:40.340
<v han>I'll pay ya back, plus a little extra. I just need a little more time.</v>

582
00:53:48.602 --> 00:53:50.718
<v han>(In english) Fifteen, jabba. Don't push it.</v>

583
00:54:02.449 --> 00:54:05.191
<v han>(In english) Jabba, you're a wonderful human being.</v>

584
00:54:14.127 --> 00:54:17.790
<v obi-wan>If the ship's as fast as he's boasting, we ought to do well.</v>

585
00:54:41.488 --> 00:54:43.103
<v luke>What a piece of junk.</v>

586
00:54:43.198 --> 00:54:45.735
<v han>She'll make .5 past light speed.</v>

587
00:54:45.826 --> 00:54:48.568
<v han>She may not look like much, but she's got it where it counts, kid.</v>

588
00:54:48.662 --> 00:54:51.654
<v han>I've made a lot of special modifications myself,</v>

589
00:54:51.748 --> 00:54:55.661
<v han>but we're a little rushed, so if you'll just get on board, we'll get outta here.</v>

590
00:55:00.841 --> 00:55:02.331
<v c-3po>Hello, sir.</v>

591
00:55:10.851 --> 00:55:12.057
<v role-stormtrooper>Which way?</v>

592
00:55:13.937 --> 00:55:15.928
<v role-stormtrooper>All right, men, load your weapons.</v>

593
00:55:18.191 --> 00:55:20.147
<v role-stormtrooper>Stop that ship. Blast them.</v>

594
00:55:29.953 --> 00:55:31.944
<v han>Chewie, get us out of here!</v>

595
00:55:33.373 --> 00:55:36.957
<v c-3po>Oh, my. I'd forgotten how much I hate space travel.</v>

596
00:55:53.351 --> 00:55:54.431
Grrr...

597
00:55:55.729 --> 00:55:57.139
<v han>Looks like an imperial cruiser.</v>

598
00:55:57.230 --> 00:55:59.141
<v han>Our passengers must be hotter than I thought.</v>

599
00:55:59.232 --> 00:56:01.018
<v han>Hold 'em off. Angle the deflector shields</v>

600
00:56:01.109 --> 00:56:03.475
<v han>while I make the calculations for the jump to light speed.</v>

601
00:56:13.163 --> 00:56:16.326
<v han>Stay sharp. There's two more comin' in. They're gonna try and cut us off.</v>

602
00:56:16.416 --> 00:56:18.816
<v luke>Why don't you outrun 'em? You said this thing was fast.</v>

603
00:56:18.877 --> 00:56:21.414
<v han>Watch your mouth or you're gonna find yourself floating home.</v>

604
00:56:21.504 --> 00:56:23.916
<v han>We'll be safe enough once we make the jump to hyperspace.</v>

605
00:56:24.007 --> 00:56:26.123
<v han>Besides, I know a few maneuvers. We'll lose 'em.</v>

606
00:56:30.889 --> 00:56:32.049
<v han>Here's where the fun begins.</v>

607
00:56:32.140 --> 00:56:33.971
<v obi-wan>How long before you can jump to light speed?</v>

608
00:56:34.059 --> 00:56:37.017
<v han>It'll take a few moments to get the coordinates from the navicomputer.</v>

609
00:56:37.103 --> 00:56:39.014
<v luke>Are you kidding? At the rate they're gaining?</v>

610
00:56:39.105 --> 00:56:41.687
<v han>Traveling through hyperspace ain't like Dustin' crops, boy.</v>

611
00:56:41.775 --> 00:56:44.266
<v han>Without precise calculations, we'd fly right through a star</v>

612
00:56:44.361 --> 00:56:48.274
<v han>or bounce too close to a supernova, and that would end your trip real quick.</v>

613
00:56:48.365 --> 00:56:50.731
<v luke>What's that flashing?</v>
<v han>We're losing a deflector shield.</v>

614
00:56:50.825 --> 00:56:53.612
<v han>Go strap yourselves in. I'm gonna make the jump to light speed.</v>

615
00:57:15.058 --> 00:57:17.720
<v motti>We've entered the alderaan system.</v>

616
00:57:17.811 --> 00:57:19.096
<v leia>Governor tarkin.</v>

617
00:57:19.187 --> 00:57:21.849
<v leia>I should have expected to find you holding vader's leash.</v>

618
00:57:22.190 --> 00:57:25.557
<v leia>I recognized your foul stench when I was brought on board.</v>

619
00:57:27.153 --> 00:57:29.018
<v tarkin>Charming to the last.</v>

620
00:57:29.823 --> 00:57:31.654
<v tarkin>You don't know how hard I found it</v>

621
00:57:31.783 --> 00:57:33.614
<v tarkin>signing the order to terminate your life.</v>

622
00:57:33.702 --> 00:57:36.660
<v leia>I'm surprised you had the courage to take the responsibility yourself.</v>

623
00:57:37.080 --> 00:57:39.822
<v tarkin>Princess Leia, before your execution,</v>

624
00:57:39.916 --> 00:57:42.373
<v tarkin>I would like you to be my guest at a ceremony</v>

625
00:57:42.460 --> 00:57:45.418
<v tarkin>that will make this battle station operational.</v>

626
00:57:45.505 --> 00:57:48.747
<v tarkin>No star system will dare oppose the emperor now.</v>

627
00:57:48.842 --> 00:57:51.083
<v leia>The more you tighten your grip, tarkin,</v>

628
00:57:51.177 --> 00:57:53.759
<v leia>the more star systems will slip through your fingers.</v>

629
00:57:53.847 --> 00:57:57.135
<v tarkin>Not after we demonstrate the power of this station.</v>

630
00:57:57.225 --> 00:58:00.683
<v tarkin>In a way, you have determined the choice of the planet</v>

631
00:58:00.770 --> 00:58:02.931
<v tarkin>that'll be destroyed first.</v>

632
00:58:03.023 --> 00:58:07.517
<v tarkin>Since you are reluctant to provide us with the location of the rebel base,</v>

633
00:58:07.610 --> 00:58:10.443
<v tarkin>I have chosen to test this station's destructive power</v>

634
00:58:10.530 --> 00:58:13.397
<v tarkin>on your home planet of alderaan.</v>

635
00:58:13.491 --> 00:58:16.278
<v leia>No. Alderaan is peaceful. We have no weapons. You can't possibly...</v>

636
00:58:16.369 --> 00:58:18.781
<v tarkin>You would prefer another target? A military target?</v>

637
00:58:18.872 --> 00:58:21.033
<v tarkin>Then name the system.</v>

638
00:58:23.001 --> 00:58:26.368
<v tarkin>I grow tired of asking this, so it will be the last time.</v>

639
00:58:27.130 --> 00:58:29.041
<v tarkin>Where is the rebel base?</v>

640
00:58:33.178 --> 00:58:34.714
<v leia>Dantooine.</v>

641
00:58:35.638 --> 00:58:36.718
<v leia>They're on dantooine.</v>

642
00:58:36.806 --> 00:58:40.219
<v tarkin>There. You see, lord vader? She can be reasonable.</v>

643
00:58:40.310 --> 00:58:43.052
<v tarkin>Continue with the operation. You may fire when ready.</v>

644
00:58:43.146 --> 00:58:45.387
<v leia>What?</v>
<v tarkin>You're far too trusting.</v>

645
00:58:45.732 --> 00:58:48.314
<v tarkin>Dantooine is too remote to make an effective demonstration.</v>

646
00:58:48.401 --> 00:58:52.485
<v tarkin>But don't worry. We will deal with your rebel friends soon enough.</v>

647
00:58:52.572 --> 00:58:53.812
Nol

648
00:58:55.700 --> 00:58:57.110
<v role-officer>commence primary ignition.</v>

649
00:59:20.391 --> 00:59:22.973
<v luke>Are you all right? What's wrong?</v>

650
00:59:23.978 --> 00:59:26.435
<v obi-wan>I felt a great disturbance in the force</v>

651
00:59:26.523 --> 00:59:29.640
<v obi-wan>as if millions of voices suddenly cried out in terror</v>

652
00:59:29.734 --> 00:59:32.066
<v obi-wan>and were suddenly silenced.</v>

653
00:59:32.153 --> 00:59:34.235
<v obi-wan>I fear something terrible has happened.</v>

654
00:59:35.907 --> 00:59:38.193
<v obi-wan>You'd better get on with your exercises.</v>

655
00:59:40.995 --> 00:59:43.532
<v han>You can forget your troubles with those imperial slugs.</v>

656
00:59:43.623 --> 00:59:46.080
<v han>I told you I'd outrun them.</v>

657
00:59:49.587 --> 00:59:51.327
<v han>Don't everybody thank me at once.</v>

658
00:59:52.132 --> 00:59:55.590
<v han>Anyway, we should be at alderaan about 0200 hours.</v>

659
01:00:03.393 --> 01:00:05.384
<v c-3po>Now be careful, r2.</v>

660
01:00:13.444 --> 01:00:14.650
Argh!

661
01:00:14.737 --> 01:00:17.319
<v c-3po>He made a fair move. Screaming about it can't help you.</v>

662
01:00:17.407 --> 01:00:19.648
<v han>Let him have it. It's not wise to upset a wookiee.</v>

663
01:00:19.742 --> 01:00:22.074
<v c-3po>But, sir, nobody worries about upsetting a droid.</v>

664
01:00:22.453 --> 01:00:24.614
<v han>That's 'cause a droid don't pull people's arms</v>

665
01:00:24.706 --> 01:00:26.742
<v han>out of their sockets when they lose.</v>

666
01:00:27.208 --> 01:00:29.415
<v han>Wookiees are known to do that.</v>

667
01:00:29.502 --> 01:00:30.617
<v chewbacca>Grrr...</v>

668
01:00:31.296 --> 01:00:32.957
<v c-3po>I see your point, sir.</v>

669
01:00:33.089 --> 01:00:36.297
<v c-3po>I suggest a new strategy, r2. Let the wookiee win.</v>

670
01:00:37.510 --> 01:00:38.875
<v chewbacca>Argh!</v>

671
01:00:54.777 --> 01:00:58.395
<v obi-wan>Remember, a jedi can feel the force flowing through him.</v>

672
01:00:59.157 --> 01:01:01.489
<v luke>You mean it controls your actions?</v>
<v obi-wan>Partially.</v>

673
01:01:01.576 --> 01:01:03.487
<v obi-wan>But it also obeys your commands.</v>

674
01:01:06.080 --> 01:01:07.570
Oh!

675
01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:10.706
<v han>Hokey religions and ancient weapons</v>

676
01:01:10.793 --> 01:01:13.000
<v han>are no match for a blaster at your side, kid.</v>

677
01:01:13.963 --> 01:01:15.578
<v luke>You don't believe in the force, do you?</v>

678
01:01:16.466 --> 01:01:18.923
<v han>Kid, I've flown from one side of this galaxy to the other.</v>

679
01:01:19.010 --> 01:01:20.591
<v han>I've seen a lot of strange stuff,</v>

680
01:01:20.678 --> 01:01:22.919
<v han>but I've never seen anything to make me believe</v>

681
01:01:23.014 --> 01:01:26.472
<v han>there's one all-powerful force controlling everything.</v>

682
01:01:27.018 --> 01:01:30.636
<v han>There's no mystical energy field controls my destiny.</v>

683
01:01:30.772 --> 01:01:33.730
<v han>It's all a lot of simple tricks and nonsense.</v>

684
01:01:33.816 --> 01:01:36.683
<v obi-wan>I suggest you try it again, Luke.</v>

685
01:01:38.238 --> 01:01:40.900
<v obi-wan>This time, let go your conscious self</v>

686
01:01:42.992 --> 01:01:45.199
<v obi-wan>and act on instinct.</v>

687
01:01:46.204 --> 01:01:49.696
<v luke>With the blast shield down, I can't see. How am I supposed to fight?</v>

688
01:01:49.791 --> 01:01:51.998
<v obi-wan>Your eyes can deceive you. Don't trust them.</v>

689
01:02:01.844 --> 01:02:03.755
<v obi-wan>Stretch out with your feelings.</v>

690
01:02:18.403 --> 01:02:20.394
<v obi-wan>You see? You can do it.</v>

691
01:02:20.989 --> 01:02:22.149
<v han>I call it luck.</v>

692
01:02:22.240 --> 01:02:24.856
<v obi-wan>In my experience, there's no such thing as luck.</v>

693
01:02:25.410 --> 01:02:27.492
<v han>Look, good against remotes is one thing.</v>

694
01:02:27.578 --> 01:02:30.741
<v han>Good against the living, that's something else.</v>

695
01:02:30.832 --> 01:02:33.414
<v han>Looks like we're coming up on alderaan.</v>

696
01:02:36.921 --> 01:02:39.663
<v luke>You know, I did feel something. I could almost see the remote.</v>

697
01:02:39.757 --> 01:02:44.547
<v obi-wan>That's good. You've taken your first step into a larger world.</v>

698
01:02:49.225 --> 01:02:50.965
<v tarkin>Yes?</v>

699
01:02:51.060 --> 01:02:52.800
<v role-officer>Our scout ships have reached dantooine.</v>

700
01:02:52.895 --> 01:02:54.760
<v role-officer>They found the remains of a rebel base,</v>

701
01:02:54.856 --> 01:02:57.268
<v role-officer>but they estimate that it has been deserted for some time.</v>

702
01:02:57.358 --> 01:03:01.067
<v role-officer>They are now conducting an extensive search of the surrounding systems.</v>

703
01:03:01.696 --> 01:03:04.278
<v tarkin>She lied. She lied to us.</v>

704
01:03:04.365 --> 01:03:08.074
<v vader>I told you she would never consciously betray the rebellion.</v>

705
01:03:09.537 --> 01:03:11.573
<v tarkin>Terminate her immediately.</v>

706
01:03:14.584 --> 01:03:17.121
<v han>Stand by, Chewie. Here we go. Cut in the sublight engines.</v>

707
01:03:19.922 --> 01:03:21.082
<v han>What the...</v>

708
01:03:22.592 --> 01:03:24.548
Aarghh arrgh!

709
01:03:24.635 --> 01:03:26.751
<v han>We've come out of hyperspace into a meteor shower,</v>

710
01:03:26.846 --> 01:03:28.177
<v han>some kind of asteroid collision.</v>

711
01:03:28.264 --> 01:03:30.346
<v han>It's not on any of the charts.</v>
<v luke>What's going on?</v>

712
01:03:30.433 --> 01:03:32.469
<v han>Our position's correct, except no alderaan.</v>

713
01:03:32.560 --> 01:03:35.427
<v luke>What do you mean? Where is it?</v>
<v han>That's what I'm trying to tell you.</v>

714
01:03:35.521 --> 01:03:37.011
<v han>It ain't there. It's been blown away.</v>

715
01:03:37.106 --> 01:03:39.438
<v luke>What? How?</v>
<v obi-wan>Destroyed by the empire.</v>

716
01:03:39.525 --> 01:03:41.891
<v han>The entire starfleet couldn't destroy the whole planet.</v>

717
01:03:41.986 --> 01:03:44.773
<v han>It'd take a thousand ships with more firepower than I've...</v>

718
01:03:46.282 --> 01:03:49.069
<v han>There's another ship coming in.</v>
<v luke>Maybe they know what happened.</v>

719
01:03:49.160 --> 01:03:50.491
<v obi-wan>It's an imperial fighter.</v>

720
01:03:52.038 --> 01:03:54.950
<v luke>It followed us.</v>
<v obi-wan>No. It's a short-range fighter.</v>

721
01:03:55.041 --> 01:03:57.498
<v han>There aren't any bases around here. Where did it come from?</v>

722
01:03:59.754 --> 01:04:02.837
<v luke>Sure is leaving in a big hurry. If they identify us, we're in trouble.</v>

723
01:04:02.924 --> 01:04:05.085
<v han>Not if I can help it. Chewie, jam its transmissions.</v>

724
01:04:05.176 --> 01:04:08.589
<v obi-wan>Let it go. It's too far out of range.</v>
<v han>Not for long.</v>

725
01:04:12.350 --> 01:04:15.683
<v obi-wan>A fighter that size couldn't get this deep into space on its own.</v>

726
01:04:15.770 --> 01:04:18.432
<v luke>He must have gotten lost, been part of a convoy or something.</v>

727
01:04:18.731 --> 01:04:21.313
<v han>He ain't gonna be around long enough to tell anybody about us.</v>

728
01:04:23.694 --> 01:04:25.730
<v luke>Look at him. He's heading for that small moon.</v>

729
01:04:25.822 --> 01:04:28.655
<v han>I think I can get him before he gets there. He's almost in range.</v>

730
01:04:29.992 --> 01:04:32.028
<v obi-wan>That's no moon.</v>

731
01:04:32.120 --> 01:04:35.487
<v obi-wan>It's a space station.</v>
<v han>It's too big to be a space station.</v>

732
01:04:38.876 --> 01:04:41.288
<v luke>I have a very bad feeling about this.</v>

733
01:04:41.379 --> 01:04:43.210
Turn the ship around.

734
01:04:43.297 --> 01:04:45.879
<v han>Yeah. I think you're right. Eull reverse.</v>

735
01:04:45.967 --> 01:04:47.628
<v han>Chewie, lock in the auxiliary power.</v>

736
01:04:52.473 --> 01:04:54.634
<v han>Chewie, lock in the auxiliary power.</v>

737
01:04:56.811 --> 01:04:58.301
<v luke>Why are we still moving towards it?</v>

738
01:04:58.396 --> 01:05:00.478
<v han>We're caught in a tractor beam. It's pulling us in.</v>

739
01:05:00.565 --> 01:05:02.226
<v luke>There's gotta be something you can do.</v>

740
01:05:02.316 --> 01:05:05.077
<v han>There's nothing I can do, kid. I'm at full power. I have to shut down.</v>

741
01:05:05.153 --> 01:05:06.859
<v han>They're not gonna get me without a fight.</v>

742
01:05:11.325 --> 01:05:14.738
<v obi-wan>You can't win, but there are alternatives to fighting.</v>

743
01:05:31.429 --> 01:05:33.511
<v role-man>Clear bay 327.</v>

744
01:05:33.598 --> 01:05:35.964
We are opening the magnetic field.

745
01:05:50.615 --> 01:05:52.901
<v role-officer>To your stations. Come with me.</v>

746
01:05:57.413 --> 01:06:01.031
<v role-man>Close all outboard shields. Close all outboard shields.</v>

747
01:06:02.210 --> 01:06:03.210
<v tarkin>Yes?</v>

748
01:06:03.294 --> 01:06:06.457
<v role-man>We've captured a freighter entering the remains of the alderaan system.</v>

749
01:06:06.547 --> 01:06:10.506
<v role-voice>Its markings match those of a ship that blasted its way out of mos eisley.</v>

750
01:06:10.593 --> 01:06:14.302
<v vader>They must be trying to return the stolen plans to the Princess.</v>

751
01:06:14.388 --> 01:06:17.175
<v vader>She may yet be of some use to us.</v>

752
01:06:22.313 --> 01:06:26.306
<v role-man>Unlock one, five, seven and nine. Release charge.</v>

753
01:06:27.818 --> 01:06:29.979
Three-one-six, report to control.

754
01:06:33.699 --> 01:06:34.939
<v role-officer>There's no one on board, sir.</v>

755
01:06:35.034 --> 01:06:37.821
<v role-officer>According to the log, the crew abandoned ship right after takeoff.</v>

756
01:06:38.538 --> 01:06:41.530
<v role-officer>It must be a decoy, sir. Several escape pods have been jettisoned.</v>

757
01:06:41.624 --> 01:06:43.489
<v vader>Did you find any droids?</v>
<v role-officer>No, sir.</v>

758
01:06:43.584 --> 01:06:45.666
<v role-officer>If there were any, they must also have jettisoned.</v>

759
01:06:45.753 --> 01:06:49.086
<v vader>Send a scanning crew aboard. I want every part of this ship checked.</v>

760
01:06:49.173 --> 01:06:50.288
<v role-officer>Yes, sir.</v>

761
01:06:50.383 --> 01:06:51.964
<v vader>I sense something,</v>

762
01:06:52.051 --> 01:06:54.884
<v vader>a presence I've not felt since...</v>

763
01:06:57.056 --> 01:06:58.967
<v role-officer>Get me a scanning crew in here on the double.</v>

764
01:06:59.058 --> 01:07:00.673
<v role-officer>I want every part of this ship checked.</v>

765
01:07:09.443 --> 01:07:11.434
There's no one here.

766
01:07:20.663 --> 01:07:22.619
<v luke>Boy, it's lucky you have these compartments.</v>

767
01:07:22.707 --> 01:07:25.824
<v han>I use them for smuggling. I never thought I'd be smuggling myself in 'em.</v>

768
01:07:25.918 --> 01:07:27.124
<v han>This is ridiculous.</v>

769
01:07:27.211 --> 01:07:29.953
<v han>Even if I could take off, I'd never get past the tractor beam.</v>

770
01:07:30.047 --> 01:07:31.162
<v obi-wan>I eave that to me.</v>

771
01:07:31.257 --> 01:07:34.465
<v han>Damn fool. I knew you were gonna say that.</v>

772
01:07:34.552 --> 01:07:38.215
<v obi-wan>Who's the more foolish, the fool or the fool who follows him?</v>

773
01:07:38.639 --> 01:07:40.175
Argh!

774
01:07:47.481 --> 01:07:52.020
<v role-stormtrooper>The ship's all yours. If the scanners pick up anything, report it immediately.</v>

775
01:07:52.903 --> 01:07:54.894
<v role-stormtrooper>All right. Let's go.</v>

776
01:08:09.128 --> 01:08:11.119
<v han>Hey, down there.</v>

777
01:08:12.882 --> 01:08:14.873
<v han>Could you give us a hand with this?</v>

778
01:08:23.267 --> 01:08:26.304
<v role-officer>Tk-421, why aren't you at your post?</v>

779
01:08:26.604 --> 01:08:28.595
<v role-officer>Tk-421, do you copy?</v>

780
01:08:41.035 --> 01:08:44.277
<v role-officer>Take over. We've got a bad transmitter. I'll see what I can do.</v>

781
01:08:47.208 --> 01:08:48.493
Grrrl

782
01:09:01.472 --> 01:09:03.554
<v luke>Between his howling and your blasting everything,</v>

783
01:09:03.641 --> 01:09:05.927
<v luke>it's a wonder the whole station doesn't know we're here.</v>

784
01:09:06.018 --> 01:09:09.306
<v han>Bring 'em on. I prefer a straight fight to all this sheakin' around.</v>

785
01:09:09.480 --> 01:09:11.186
<v c-3po>We've found the computer outlet, sir.</v>

786
01:09:11.273 --> 01:09:14.310
<v obi-wan>Plug in. He should be able to interpret the entire imperial network.</v>

787
01:09:25.705 --> 01:09:29.072
<v c-3po>He says he's found the controls to the power beam that's holding the ship here.</v>

788
01:09:29.166 --> 01:09:31.748
<v c-3po>He'll try to make the precise location appear on the monitor.</v>

789
01:09:32.420 --> 01:09:36.333
<v c-3po>The tractor beam is coupled to the main reactor in seven locations.</v>

790
01:09:36.424 --> 01:09:39.757
<v c-3po>A power loss at one of the terminals will allow the ship to leave.</v>

791
01:09:42.179 --> 01:09:45.421
<v obi-wan>I don't think you boys can help. I must go alone.</v>

792
01:09:45.516 --> 01:09:48.974
<v han>Whatever you say. I've done more than I bargained for on this trip already.</v>

793
01:09:49.103 --> 01:09:50.218
<v luke>I want to go with you.</v>

794
01:09:50.312 --> 01:09:53.145
<v obi-wan>Be patient, Luke. Stay and watch over the droids.</v>

795
01:09:53.232 --> 01:09:54.642
<v obi-wan>They must be delivered safely</v>

796
01:09:54.734 --> 01:09:58.443
<v obi-wan>or other star systems will suffer the same fate as alderaan.</v>

797
01:09:58.529 --> 01:10:01.862
<v obi-wan>Your destiny lies along a different path from mine.</v>

798
01:10:05.536 --> 01:10:07.276
<v obi-wan>The force will be with you...</v>

799
